Update deletion to GitHub
✅ Step 1: Go to your repo folder

Inside wherever your repo exists (container or VPS):

cd /root/jenkins_sandbox_home

(or your repo path)

✅ Step 2: Check status
git status

You should see something like:

deleted: filename.txt
✅ Step 3: Stage the deletion
git add .

👉 This tells Git: “yes, I want to delete this file in the repo”

(Alternative specific way:)

git rm filename.txt
✅ Step 4: Commit the change
git commit -m "Removed unused file"
✅ Step 5: Push to GitHub
git push origin main
🔥 DONE

Your file is now:
✅ Deleted locally
✅ Deleted in GitHub repo

⚠️ COMMON ISSUES
❌ “nothing to commit”

Means:

File wasn’t tracked by Git
👉 Fix:
git add -A
git commit -m "Sync changes"
